<item>
            <title>[LU-20772] Remove broken TCP backoff support</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20772</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The TCP_BACKOFF_INIT and TCP_BACKOFF_MAX socket options were never part of mainline Linux. They come from the &quot;Customizable TCP backoff patch&quot; that Ben Woodard and Brian Behlendorf posted to netdev in September 2006 for LLNL&apos;s oversubscribed gigE clusters, where thousands of TCP streams backed off in lock step:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160; &#160; &#160; &lt;a href=&quot;https://lwn.net/Articles/202398/&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://lwn.net/Articles/202398/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This support is definitely broken and unused at this point.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
